------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATH / MODULE RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated paths do not match this repo; they are corrected to the
repo's real, gate-compliant locations (evidence cited), NOT worked around:

  1. Gradle module: prompt says `:app:` -> real module is `:android`.
     Evidence: apps/android/settings.gradle.kts L33-36
       include(":android"); project(":android").projectDir = file("app")
       ("every P3/A* prompt gate addresses `:android:`").
     `:app:assembleRelease` fails with "project 'app' not found"; `:android:` is used.

  2. Source location: prompt says
       apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/AlertFeedWidget
     The real app package root is `io.teslasync.android` under src/main/java, and
     `com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets` cannot back any valid Kotlin package
     (hyphen + wrong root). The repo's detekt rule InvalidPackageDeclaration
     (active, warningsAsErrors=true) REQUIRES package == directory, so the
     templated path is rejected by the repo's own quality gate. Files are placed
     at the idiomatic, rule-compliant location:
       apps/android/app/src/main/java/io/teslasync/android/dashboardwidgets/alertfeed/
     package io.teslasync.android.dashboardwidgets.alertfeed
     (mirrors the Windows sibling namespace TeslaSync.App.DashboardWidgets).
     The placeholder scan + commit below target this real path.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILES (the AlertFeedWidget surface bundle + its tests)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
main/.../dashboardwidgets/alertfeed/
  AlertFeedWidgetModel.kt      pure model: AlertFeedSize (isWide/isTall/maxItems),
                               AlertFeedRegistration (id/category/slug/sizes/bounds),
                               AlertDrillthrough (+SIGNAL_TO_PAGE port, href),
                               AlertRowSubtitle, AlertFeedRow, AlertFeedProjection
                               (newest-first sort + maxItems cap), relative-time +
                               content-description helpers.
  AlertFeedWidgetSource.kt     AlertFeedSource seam (web useAlerts / Windows
                               IAlertFeedSource) + bindings to the shared S7
                               NotificationsRepository and S8 NotificationsStore.
  AlertFeedWidgetViewModel.kt  state holder over BaseFeedViewModel.asUiState;
                               refresh/retry re-fetch; one-shot view.opened (P1/S11).
  AlertFeedWidget.kt           Compose view: shell (Card) + header (Bell + title +
                               DataFreshness + refresh) + per-state body; 4 @Preview.
test/.../dashboardwidgets/alertfeed/
  AlertFeedWidgetModelTest.kt      12 tests (projection/drillthrough/registration/a11y).
  AlertFeedWidgetViewModelTest.kt  8 tests (state matrix/refresh/retry/diagnostics).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY EVIDENCE (web -> native, file:symbol)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[data]   useAlerts            -> AlertFeedSource.stream() bound to NotificationsStore.alerts()
                                  / NotificationsRepository.alerts() (AlertFeedWidgetSource.kt)
[data]   useNotifications     -> shared io.teslasync.shared.core...NotificationsStore (S8)
[i18n]   widget.alertFeed     -> R.string.translation_widget_alertFeed ("Alert Feed")
[i18n]   widget.noAlerts      -> R.string.translation_widget_noAlerts ("No alerts yet")
[i18n]   severity labels      -> translation_notifications_alertStudio_severity_{info,warn,critical},
                                  translation_Success  (AlertFeedWidget.kt severityLabel)
[logic]  isWide/isTall/maxItems (12/8/5) -> AlertFeedSize (AlertFeedWidgetModel.kt)
[logic]  SEVERITY normalize + icon       -> normalizeSeverity/severityGlyph/severityColor (shared comps)
[logic]  getAlertDrillthroughHref        -> AlertDrillthrough.forAlert/href (1:1 SIGNAL_TO_PAGE port)
[logic]  WidgetEventFeed sort+cap+relTime-> AlertFeedProjection + alertRelativeTimeLabel
[state]  loading  -> Skeleton rows (a11y: translation_a11y_loading)
[state]  content  -> LazyColumn of severity-iconed rows w/ drill-through + TalkBack desc
[state]  empty    -> EmptyState(Bell, "No alerts yet")
[state]  error    -> QueryError(classifyQueryError(...)) + Retry
[state]  stale    -> cached rows + DataFreshness stale chip (UiState.stale)
[state]  offline  -> cached rows + DataFreshness error chip (UiState.isOffline)
[a11y]   row contentDescription, refresh button label, heading semantics, >=48dp targets
[telem]  view.opened slug=AlertFeedWidget -> AlertFeedWidgetViewModel.onViewOpened (P1/S11)

Note on tests: UI/state coverage is exercised as JVM unit tests over the state
holder + pure projection + a11y/diagnostics builders (the gate runs
:android:testReleaseUnitTest only; instrumented Compose UI tests need an emulator
the gate does not start). The stateless AlertFeedWidgetContent + 4 @Preview render
each state (loading/content/empty/error) for screenshot/visual verification.

